C/ DB id 14 (mmwsnp_vector_forces_newline): a VECTOR/MATRIX WRITE
C/ argument always starts a fresh line, even when a preceding item on
C/ the same WRITE statement would otherwise leave room on the current
C/ line -- confirmed against RUNASM/MMWSNP.asm ("SINGLE PRECISION
C/ VECTOR/MATRIX OUTPUT INTERFACE"), whose own OLOOP unconditionally
C/ does ACALL SKIP then ACALL COLUMN(1) before writing each row.

  T:
  PROGRAM;
     DECLARE V VECTOR(3) INITIAL(1.0, 2.0, 3.0);
     WRITE(6) 'SUM=', V;
Y %SVCI(0);
  CLOSE T;
